From d005d1bdba7183f7c40ba7be185980f885517796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: whn09 <wanghenan09@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:31:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] serve: Mooncake Transfer Engine KV transport for the
 prefill/decode split (--kv-transport mooncake)

Stacked on #197 (pd_server.py / pd_transfer.py), which moves the prefilled KV blocks and SWA
state PE -> CE as pinned host buffers over TCP. --kv-transport mooncake keeps that flow and
control socket, and replaces the data plane with a Mooncake TransferEngine:

- deepinfer/hicache/pd_mooncake.py: GpuArena (one registered device buffer per rank, first-fit
  regions; cuMemAlloc like the KV pools, since expandable_segments memory has no cudaIpc
  handle) and MooncakeLink (TransferEngine with P2PHANDSHAKE metadata, register_memory,
  transfer_sync_write).
- PDTransfer.export_into / admit accept device buffers: the PE exports a sequence straight
  into an arena region (state included, no extra staging) and the CE admits from its arena.
- pd_server.py: MC_MAGIC header -> CE reserves an arena region and replies {addr, segment}
  (or busy -> retry) -> one contiguous write -> go/ok. Writes are retried, then the region is
  sent over the TCP path, so a failing peer cannot strand a request. TCP is unchanged and is
  also the fallback when the PE arena is full.
- --mooncake-protocol nvlink_intra (default, one host) or rdma/efa across hosts.
- serve/README.md: usage; containers must share IPC and PID namespaces (--pid=host).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
